# Picnic Letter
The picnic's letter:  the same rules and details for everyone, then what's yours alone.
Each part shows only what its reader may see:  your own shifts, your own invitations.


## A shift you signed up for

<spell-more-of "listing">
	<draw>
		<label class="shift">{its shift}</label>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>


## Your invitations' count, from your inbox

<spell-more-of "message">
	<draw>
		<text class="count">{its text}</text>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>


## The letter

<spell-app "picnic letter">
	<property "shifts">every listing where its person is them</>
	<property "counts">every message where its thread is "invitations"</>

	<draw>
		<container class="letter">
			<stack>
				<header size="large">The Picnic:  your letter</header>
				<segment class="details">
					<header size="medium">The day</header>
					<text paragraph>Saturday from 9 to 4, at Riverside Park, by the bandstand.  Bring a chair, and something to share.</text>
					<text paragraph>Your ticket's guest gets into the attendees' space once an organizer confirms it:  the map and the day's news are there.</text>
				</segment>
				<segment class="your-shifts">
					<header size="medium">You have signed up for these shifts</header>
					<stack class="shifts" direction="horizontal" spacing="sm" wrap>
						<for listing in its shifts loading="Reading the sheet">
							<empty><text color="grey">No shifts yet:  sign up on the sheet.</text></empty>
							<failed><text color="grey">Sign in to see your shifts.</text></failed>
						</for>
					</stack>
				</segment>
				<segment class="your-invitations">
					<header size="medium">Your invitations</header>
					<stack class="counts" spacing="sm">
						<for message in its counts>
							<empty><text color="grey">You haven't asked for any yet.</text></empty>
							<failed><text color="grey">Sign in to see your invitations.</text></failed>
						</for>
					</stack>
				</segment>
			</stack>
		</container>
	</draw>
</spell-app>
